{"data":{"body":"[P1] Allocate the operation ID atomically\n\n`_peek_next_operation_id()` and `_create_step_id()` lock the counter separately. Two threads sharing a `DurableContext` can therefore both construct identifiers for step N; the second thread increments to N+1 but still checkpoints operation N, causing duplicate IDs and cross-operation checkpoint consumption. Atomically reserve the ID first, then make `_replay_aware` inspect that allocated ID. Add a barrier-based shared-context test.","comment_node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPsIIsM7pAur9","finding_digest":"76d3cd8714edb04db8f969e8af7f3b0cb5a3420c11caaa5a9c1640882711c7ec","finding_id":"arf_v1_o3j43byu5wye3ohznhuk67z3bs","finding_key":"context.py::durablecontext._operation_replay_aware::atomic-operation-id-allocation","identity_key":"context.py::durablecontext._operation_replay_aware::atomic-operation-id-allocation","line":596,"observation_digest":"30a29f584550d5741cfdb5fe81ea96c1f11d4454025e2e440b26fe05489b0dc8","observation_id":"aro_v1_gcrj6wcfkdkxihh5wx7id2uwyh","path":"packages/aws-durable-execution-sdk-python/src/aws_durable_execution_sdk_python/context.py","prior_finding_id":"","published_at":"2026-09-01T23:18:10Z","review_id":"arr_v1_37gebalm6wiyykwqja2happijm","reviewed_base_sha":"ea0bc35cef49b694999c0c2578ad3c76a381f844","reviewed_head_sha":"a2233e9a9a3d88aedb29fe9b7dcc775f3b056252","reviewer":"codex","start_line":596,"suggestion_id":""},"pull_request":{"number":698},"record_id":"art_v1_s32sejbhvvic6tpixf56crld6u","record_type":"finding_observed","recorded_at":"2026-09-01T23:18:10Z","repository":{"full_name":"aws/aws-durable-execution-sdk-python","id":1052903600},"schema_version":1}
